{"title":"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick,_fast,_easy!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick, fast, easy!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d50005de672f42f4b8c5925e806246e441dcd1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{tetromino}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" /> consists of four squares connected along their edges. There are five possible tetromino shapes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, shown below, which can be rotated or flipped over. Three tetrominoes are used to completely cover a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/f/3ef2bd2ffcfe42b7352efb430653bcc8530751fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> rectangle. At least one of the tiles is an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> tile. What are the other two tiles?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/55361328ba3a49e231113919181a6ee00db0b887.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(12);  add(grid(1,4)); label(&quot;I&quot;, (0.5,-1));  add(shift((5,0)) * grid(2,2)); label(&quot;O&quot;, (6,-1));  add(shift((11,0)) * grid(1,3)); add(shift((11,0)) * grid(2,1)); label(&quot;L&quot;, (12,-1));  add(shift((18,0)) * grid(1,1)); add(shift((17,1)) * grid(3,1)); label(&quot;T&quot;, (18.5,-1));  add(shift((25,1)) * grid(2,1)); add(shift((24,0)) * grid(2,1)); label(&quot;S&quot;, (25.5,-1));  add(shift((12,-6)) * grid(4,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"542\" height=\"202\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86689d4065772bd181f58ac7ee00fe8498f15ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da493a22d70ea013d06a6c1839b26705346b1db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L\\qquad \\textbf{(B)} I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e0133f20bbb35e5494402608e0f3978c960d272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T\\qquad \\textbf{(C)} L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87ffe11c49e2715c698fdf8da5a80db54f92a04b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/d/06da53d8de3b0ee0ef08ee764cc4b6c49250ef64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/f/3ef2bd2ffcfe42b7352efb430653bcc8530751fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> rectangle allows for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible places to put the S piece, with each possible placement having an inverted version. One of the cases looks like this:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f906cc598e2acb299497c759688b48dc8e40baaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] path x = (0,0)--(0,2)--(1,2)--(1,3)--(2,3)--(2,1)--(1,1)--(1,0)--cycle; fill(x, rgb(0,30,0)); add(grid(4,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"188\" />\nAs you can see, there is a hole in the top left corner of the board, which would be impossible to fill using the tetrominos. There are three cases in which a hole isn't created; the S lies flat in the bottom left corner, it lies flat in the top right corner, or it stands upright in the center. All three tilings are shown below.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31f10e2603ccc46e0fd9c565e52f6e3b6c89c6f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] path z1 = (2,0)--(3,0)--(3,2)--(2,2)--(2,3)--(1,3)--(1,1)--(2,1)--cycle; path z2 = (0,0)--(2,0)--(2,1)--(1,1)--(1,3)--(0,3)--cycle; path z3 = (2,3)--(4,3)--(4,0)--(3,0)--(3,2)--(2,2)--cycle; fill(z1, rgb(0,30,0)); fill(z2, rgb(127,80,0)); fill(z3, rgb(127,100,0)); add(grid(4,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"188\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6577c9df5c364edc8d78af08d5a68c2d33a6e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] path y1 = (0,0)--(2,0)--(2,1)--(3,1)--(3,2)--(1,2)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle; path y2 = (0,1)--(1,1)--(1,2)--(3,2)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle; path y3 = (2,0)--(4,0)--(4,3)--(3,3)--(3,1)--(2,1)--cycle; fill(y1, rgb(0,30,0)); fill(y2, rgb(127,80,0)); fill(y3, rgb(127,100,0)); add(grid(4,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"188\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e210947e5413e15b8ed3bbb22327bdfedb8234c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] path w1 = (1,1)--(3,1)--(3,2)--(4,2)--(4,3)--(2,3)--(2,2)--(1,2)--cycle; path w2 = (0,0)--(0,3)--(2,3)--(2,2)--(1,2)--(1,0)--cycle; path w3 = (1,0)--(4,0)--(4,2)--(3,2)--(3,1)--(1,1)--cycle; fill(w1, rgb(0,30,0)); fill(w2, rgb(127,80,0)); fill(w3, rgb(127,100,0)); add(grid(4,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"188\" />\nFor each of the inverted cases, the L pieces can be inverted along with the S piece. Because the only cases that fill the rectangle after the S is placed are the ones that use two L pieces, the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4da511ae45cd28ce9ce6dbfa32aca1b01fdc117.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~L \\ and \\ L}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"113\" height=\"30\" />.\n~bubby617\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_.28First_fully_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=zQzviZTDWMMlueEJ&amp;t=2381\">https://youtu.be/VUL0T0YEAHk?si=zQzviZTDWMMlueEJ&amp;t=2381</a>\n~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=mhn50YKL4_Yo1PH6&amp;t=965\">https://youtu.be/VP7g-s8akMY?si=mhn50YKL4_Yo1PH6&amp;t=965</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Thinking_Feet\">Video Solution 1 by Thinking Feet</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Thinking Feet\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988\">https://youtu.be/PKMpTS6b988</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick.2C_fast.2C_easy.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick,_fast,_easy!)\">Video Solution(Quick, fast, easy!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick, fast, easy!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/fdG7EDW_7xk\">https://youtu.be/fdG7EDW_7xk</a> \n</p><p>~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EB-Uaexj9-4&amp;t=860s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EB-Uaexj9-4&amp;t=860s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_.28AIME_Qualifier.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1fvuP6TECE/?spm_id_from=333.1387.upload.video_card.click\">https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1fvuP6TECE/?spm_id_from=333.1387.upload.video_card.click</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8\" title=\"2025 AMC 8\">2025 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2025 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017045752\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 191/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2272/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5269/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.377      1 -total\n 57.74%    7.147      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 40.57%    5.021      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:27111:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017045752 and revision id 289179. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}